For the next case with rawValue of -2, I need to confirm that filteredValue becomes -2.0 since sampleCount is 1 and the buffer now contains only this new value. The fix involves adding a bufferValid flag to track when the buffer has been populated, then updating filteredValue only when bufferValid is true, otherwise preserving the last computed value. I should also verify that writeIndex resets properly on re-enable and handle the boundary case where sampleCount reaches zero.

